@startuml 08-projection-parity

title Parity by construction - one write path, regenerable projections

database "Git (system of record)\nspdd/memory/lessons.jsonl\nspdd/memory/registry.jsonl" as git
database "SQLite cache (opt-in)\n.sdlc/index.sqlite\nschema v5" as sqlite
database "Guide DICE (default)\nNeo4j graph\nspdd-projection-v3" as guide
participant "sdlc-engine\ncontext parity [--repair]" as parity

git -> sqlite : sdlc.sh db rebuild\n(ledger + registry + canvases\n+ governance docs)
git -> guide : projection API\n(re-project on accept\nor on demand)

parity -> git : accepted record ids
parity -> sqlite : lesson rows + claims
parity -> guide : projection stats / ids
parity -> parity : compare id sets and counts
alt drift detected
  parity -> sqlite : --repair: rebuild from ledger
  parity -> guide : --repair: re-project ledger
end

note over git, guide
  Backends never receive independent writes.
  Delete sqlite or the graph at any time -
  both regenerate from the committed JSONL.
  Default backends: git + guide;
  sqlite via CONTEXT_BACKENDS opt-in.
end note

@enduml
